  "notes": "Village with modified cash basis governmental funds and accrual enterprise funds (Water, Sewer, Garbage). Governmental receipts/disbursements are the Total Governmental Funds column of the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances (p5). Cash-basis beginning/ending cash are the total fund balances (813,641 / 844,199; p5); balance sheet total assets 850,010 = fund balances 844,199 + payroll withholding 5,811. Transfers: General Fund +157,785 from Sales Tax Fund (-157,785); the Total column shows none, recorded as equal in and out. Business-type receipts/disbursements from the Proprietary Funds statement (p7) total column; balance is net position (accrual). Proprietary cash flows from the Statement of Cash Flows - Proprietary Funds (p8) Total column (accrual enterprise funds); no noncapital financing section printed. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (mixes modified cash governmental and accrual business-type); kept because its governmental column includes capital assets (Land, CIP, other capital assets) and differs from the governmental funds balance sheet (p4). Attempt 2 (targeted re-check): Street Fund budget 'Other' 124 is Interest Income (the statement p5 prints it as Street Fund interest income 124); utility bills line tagged function utilities. Intergovernmental lines are not broken down anywhere in the report, so no state aid split. General Fund detail recorded from the department combining statement (p12, more detailed); the General Fund budget schedule (p9) is not recorded to avoid double counting (its function lines: general government 129,208 includes capital outlay 5,163). Street Fund bond proceeds and transfers have budget only, actual dash, not recorded. Keno fund had no activity. Attempt 3 (charges-for-services re-check 2026-10-29): business-type 'Sales' 409,482 is the utility sales of the Water, Sewer and Garbage funds (p7) -> Utility Charges; General Fund Cemetery department charges for services 1,250 -> Cemetery Fees and Park department 5,525 -> Recreation Fees (p12); the statement's 'Charges for services' 8,275 (p5) is a genuine charges line and stays charges for services. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
